From: Kettle Linux
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6dsp-lpass-clocks: set drvdata before registering the clocks

An ADSP restart froze SM8750 handhelds (AYN Odin 3, Odin 3 Portal). When
the ADSP goes down, q6prm's clocks are unregistered while the LPASS
codec macros still hold them prepared ("unregistering prepared clock:
LPASS_HW_MACRO" and others), and the clock core keeps those children,
prepared, as orphans. When the ADSP is back, q6dsp_clock_dev_probe()
registers the new clocks; registering one re-parents the orphans and
prepares it at once. clk_q6dsp_prepare() then reads the provider's
drvdata, which the probe only set after the loop: a NULL dereference
in clk_q6dsp_prepare() under the clock prepare lock, from the
pdr_notifier work, and every later clock operation waits on that lock.

Set drvdata before the first clock is registered.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -145,6 +145,12 @@
 	cc->desc = desc;
 	cc->dev = dev;
 	q6dsp_clks = desc->clks;
+	/*
+	 * Before the clocks are registered: registering one adopts orphans left
+	 * prepared by the previous instance (after an ADSP restart) and
+	 * prepares it at once, and the clock ops find cc through drvdata.
+	 */
+	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_clks; i++) {
 		unsigned int id = q6dsp_clks[i].clk_id;
@@ -174,12 +180,6 @@
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider(dev, q6dsp_of_clk_hw_get, cc);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
-	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
-
-	return 0;
+	return devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider(dev, q6dsp_of_clk_hw_get, cc);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6dsp_clock_dev_probe);
